6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium
(including a physical distribution medium) in one of the following
ways:

i) The Corresponding Source is included in the physical product
or on a physical distribution medium in a machine-readable format.
ii) The Corresponding Source is included in the physical product
or on a physical distribution medium in a machine-readable format.

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
written offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as
long as you offer spare parts or customer service for that product,
to give anyone who possesses the object code a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium in a machine-
readable format (i.e., on a CD-ROM or other medium capable of
storing the information) at no charge, or at no greater charge than
the cost of performing this conduit.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium (i.e., on a CD-ROM)
in a machine-readable format.

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (gratis or for a charge), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
further charge. You need not require recipients to copy the
Corresponding Source for themselves.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer transmission, provided
you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source and the
Corresponding Source for the works on which the object code is based
is available to the general public at no charge.

A separable portion of the object code, whose source code is excluded
from the Corresponding Source as a System Library, need not be
included in the above conveyance, and you need not offer to convey
that separable portion's Corresponding Source.

