copyright holder is reinstated (a) provisionally, unless and until
the copyright holder explicitly and finally terminates your license,
and (b) permanently, if the copyright holder fails to notify you of
the termination by reasonable means prior to 60 days after the
cessation.

Moreover, your license from a particular copyright holder is
reinstated permanently if the copyright holder notifies you of the
termination by reasonable means, and you do not resume violation
within 30 days of receiving the notification.

Termination of your rights under this License does not terminate the
licenses of other parties who have received copies, or rights, from
you under this License. If your rights have been terminated and you
have not permanently lost them, you may receive a new license from
the same copyright holder, if the copyright holder is willing to grant
it, but this will be a different license from the one you had.

